ent implementation calls `queue.sync` from inside a work item already on the background queue, which is fine, but it captures `self` (the index) weakly. However, the index is owned by the cache and lives as long as it does, so `weak self` is overly cautious but correct. Let me verify the debounced save doesn't cause a deadlock: the work item runs on `DispatchQueue.global`, then calls `queue.sync` (the serial cache queue). That's safe since the work item is not on the serial queue. Good.\n\nLet me do a final review of all files to confirm correctness:","type":"text"},{"id":"toolu_01FNrkqjmNqCHHHxMzyzs3HK","input":{"path":"/workspace/Sources/LRUFileCache/LRUFileCacheIndex.swift","reason":"Verify final state of the index file"},"name":"read_file","type":"tool_use"},{"id":"toolu_012XkcEWr8btr8TtKzyYskQL","input":{"path":"/workspace/Sources/LRUFileCache/LRUFileCache.swift","reason":"Verify final state of the main cache file"},"name":"read_file","type":"tool_use"}],"role":"assistant"},{"content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FNrkqjmNqCHHHxMzyzs3HK","is_error":false,"content":[{"text":"    1\timport Foundation\n    2\t\n    3\tstruct IndexEntry: Codable {\n    4\t    let key: String\n    5\t    var fileName: String\n    6\t    var lastAccessedDate: Date\n    7\t    var byteSize: Int\n    8\t}\n    9\t\n   10\tfinal class LRUFileCacheIndex {\n   11\t    private(set) var entries: [String: IndexEntry] = [:]\n   12\t    private(set) var totalBytes: Int = 0\n   13\t\n   14\t    private let indexFileURL: URL\n   15\t    private var debouncedSaveWorkItem: DispatchWorkItem?\n   16\t    private let queue: DispatchQueue\n   17\t\n   18\t    init(cacheDirectory: URL, queue: DispatchQueue) {\n   19\t        self.indexFileURL = cacheDirectory.appendingPathComponent(\"index.json\")\n   20\t        self.queue = queue\n   21\t        load()\n   22\t    }\n   23\t\n   24\t    private func load() {\n   25\t        guard let data = try? Data(contentsOf: indexFileURL) else { return }\n   26\t     